# Databases (dev SQLite files must never be committed)
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
# Passing ":memory:" as a filesystem path rather than as the URL
# `sqlite:///:memory:` creates a real database file with that literal name.
# One was committed with live capture rows in it; database/engine.py now
# rejects the bare form, and this stops a stray file being committed again.
:memory:

